    "title": "The place page: a quieter photo corner, what's in the photo, the numbers always shown, Plan a trip here",
    "why": "Jason, 2026-11-19, approved (reviewed by the session manager): \"1. maybe we have a way for the view to see the location/url of the subject. 2. maybe a way to create a trip right from here. 3. the social numbers should always be present shouldnt they? 4. Maybe a ... tool kit for things?\" The photo viewer names what's in the photo (its page, See on the map, Copy link) and shows that place's views, likes and comments; views show at 0; ⋯ on the engage bar holds See on the map, Directions (a street that isn't private), Plan a trip here (the place's ready-made journeys, then the Trip Planner set to it), Add to a trip (coming), Save contact, Suggest an edit and Report. A business with only a mailbox gets no Directions on its own page either. No new tables. Then Jason's change, on his phone's screenshot of a listing: \"Should share, add a photo, etc be added to minimize how much real-estate is used on hero.\" The hero's corner keeps views, likes and comments and ⋯; Share, QR, Share a photo and Save to Address Book go into ⋯ in words, and nothing the page already shows beside its card is repeated (a listing's QR and contact buttons had shown twice).",
